{"id":"u-4290b03e-5153-4290-9c8a-d118ba178edb","src":"community","title":"Total Body Hypertrophy","author":"Brownbear","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/zFoPAG-total-hypertrophy","desc":"This four-day program is designed for lifters who want to prioritize muscle growth without spending hours in the gym.\n\nThe philosophy is simple: keep the compounds, prioritize hypertrophy, and eliminate unnecessary fatigue.\n\nHow It Works\n\nThe program follows a four-day split:\n\nMonday – Upper Pull: Back, rear delts, and biceps\n\nTuesday – Lower Anterior: Quads, calves, and complementary hamstring work\n\nThursday – Upper Push: Chest, shoulders, and triceps\n\nSaturday – Lower Posterior: Glutes, hamstrings, and complementary quad work\n\nWeek A/B Rotation\n\nThe program alternates between two workout variations every week.\n\nWeek A\n\nUpper Pull: Assisted pull-up emphasis\n\nLower Anterior: Barbell squats\n\nUpper Push: Barbell bench press\n\nLower Posterior: Hip thrust emphasis\n\nWeek B\n\nUpper Pull: Barbell row emphasis\n\nLower Anterior: Barbell squats\n\nUpper Push: Barbell overhead press\n\nLower Posterior: Deadlift emphasis\n\nAfter Week B, return to Week A and repeat.\n\nEach session begins with a compound movement followed by targeted accessory exercises.\n\nStructure\n\nCompound foundations: Traditional lifts remain central, supporting continued strength progression alongside muscle growth.\n\nIntelligent fatigue management: Train complementary muscle groups on different days. Leg curls on quad-focused days and leg extensions on posterior-focused days provide additional stimulus without another demanding compound movement.\n\nBalanced development: All major muscle groups receive attention, with additional emphasis on back, arms, and glutes.\n\nProgressive Overload\n\nThe program uses double progression.\n\nFor all exercises, increase repetitions until all three sets reach the upper limit of the rep range with controlled technique and the intended effort. Then increase the weight slightly and repeat.\n\nIntensity targets:\n\nMost compound lifts: 1–2 reps in reserve (RIR)\n\nSquats and deadlifts: Approximately 2 RIR\n\nIsolation exercises: 0–2 RIR\n\nRest 2–3 minutes between demanding compound sets and 60–90 seconds between isolation sets. Superset compatible accessories when practical.\n\nChoose exercise variations based on skill, preference, comfort, or equipment availability.\n\nRecovery and Progress\n\nTrain four days per week, aiming for approximately 60 minutes per session. Track weights and repetitions, prioritize good technique, and progress consistently.\n\nMonitor recovery and reduce volume or deload if accumulated fatigue persistently affects performance.\n\nTrain hard. Recover well. Build muscle.","level":["Novice","Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-11-01T08:08:43.807Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Upper Pull A","Lower Anterior","Upper Push A","Lower Posterior A"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Pull-Up (Assisted)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Barbell Row","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Chest Supported Row (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Bayesian Curl","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hammer Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Face Pull","sets":[{"r":15,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Leg Curl","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Leg Press","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Seated Calf Raise","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Tricep Pushdown (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Plank","sets":[{"sec":60,"x":2}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Seated Overhead Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Chest Fly (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Tricep Dip (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"O